<!-- CHAPTER 1 -->
<h2>1. Introduction & Academic Architecture</h2>
<p>
  <strong>ChemBuddy</strong> is an advanced, offline-first mobile application designed specifically to eliminate the academic friction experienced by Master of Science (MSc) Chemistry postgraduates. Developed by <strong>Prajwal A Kambar</strong>, it merges rigorous chemoinformatics, high-precision spectroscopy solvers, attendance predictive mathematics, and state-of-the-art generative AI into a unified laboratory and classroom companion.
</p>

<h3>Core Engineering Principles</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>100% Offline Core:</strong> Attendance calculations, timetable intelligence, 16 postgrad calculators, Woodward-Hoffmann pericyclic selection rules, spectroscopy databases, and reaction prediction algorithms function entirely on-device without internet connectivity.</li>
  <li><strong>Scientific Rigor:</strong> All formulas, mechanisms, spectroscopic chemical shifts, and thermodynamic equations strictly adhere to IUPAC standards and standard graduate textbooks (Silverstein, Pavia, March, Clayden).</li>
  <li><strong>Student Privacy & Local Ownership:</strong> Student profiles, attendance logs, notes, and uploaded PDFs reside securely in encrypted local Hive boxes on your device. Zero telemetry or surveillance.</li>
  <li><strong>Dark Laboratory Ergonomics:</strong> The UI utilizes high-contrast deep purple (<code>#0A0914</code>) and cyan (<code>#06B6D4</code>) palettes engineered to preserve dark-adapted vision in laser labs and darkrooms.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 2 -->
<h2>2. Installation, Android Permissions & Initial Setup</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Download Release APK:</strong> Download <code>ChemBuddy-v3.5.1-by-Prajwal-A-Kambar.apk</code> from the official GitHub Releases page.</li>
  <li><strong>Enable Unknown Sources:</strong> In Android Settings, navigate to <em>Security &rarr; Install Unknown Apps</em> and allow your browser or file manager to install APKs.</li>
  <li><strong>Grant Essential Permissions:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> Required for the 8:30 AM Timetable Briefing, 30-min class alerts, and 8:00 PM Psychology Facts.</li>
      <li><strong>Alarms & Reminders (Android 12+):</strong> Required so that scheduled class notifications fire with exact timing.</li>
      <li><strong>Battery Optimization:</strong> Set to <em>"Unrestricted"</em> so Android Doze does not suppress morning notifications.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Profile Initialization:</strong> On first launch, enter your Name, College/University, Semester, and Specialization (Organic, Inorganic, Physical, or Analytical).</li>
</ol>

<!-- CHAPTER 3: FLAGSHIP FEATURE -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>3. 🌟 Ask ChemBuddy AI — The Chemistry Intelligence Engine (FLAGSHIP FEATURE)</h2>

<div class="callout callout-info">
  <div class="callout-title">💡 Flagship Feature Spotlight: ChemBuddy AI</div>
  <strong>ChemBuddy AI</strong> is your 24/7 MSc Chemistry Research & Exam Companion. Accessible via the <strong>Ask AI</strong> bottom navigation tab or the Home Screen action card, it connects directly to Google Gemini models (with intelligent offline fallbacks) and provides 9 specialized academic modes, chemistry-aware speech recognition, and instant active recall flashcard generation.
</div>

<div class="two-column">
  <div class="column-text">
    <h3>3.1 Overview of the ChemBuddy AI Interface</h3>
    <p>
      The Ask ChemBuddy screen is designed to behave like an interactive academic interview with a senior chemistry professor. Key components include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Horizontal Mode Scroller:</strong> Tap between 9 specialized AI modes instantly.</li>
      <li><strong>Chemistry Speech-to-Text:</strong> Tap the pulsing purple microphone button to dictate questions verbally. ChemBuddy automatically normalizes spoken phrases (e.g. converting "SN1" to <em>S<sub>N</sub>1</em>, "Huckel rule" to <em>4n+2</em>, and "H-NMR" to <em><sup>1</sup>H NMR</em>).</li>
      <li><strong>KaTeX Equation Box:</strong> Mathematical and chemical expressions are formatted in crisp, textbook LaTeX notation.</li>
      <li><strong>Electron Pushing & Curved Arrows:</strong> Step-by-step mechanism breakdowns detail electron displacement from nucleophile to electrophile.</li>
      <li><strong>1-Tap Flashcard Generation:</strong> Save any AI response directly into your spaced repetition flashcard deck with a single tap.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="column-image">
    <div class="screenshot-container">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64," class="screenshot-img" alt="Ask ChemBuddy AI Interface">
      <div class="screenshot-caption">Figure 3.1: Ask ChemBuddy AI Interface with 5-Mark Exam Rubric mode, KaTeX math, and step-by-step electron pushing notation.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

