<h3>3.3 Chemistry Speech-to-Text Normalization</h3>
<p>
  When dictating via the microphone button (<code>🎙️</code>), ChemBuddy passes speech through the proprietary <code>ChemistryTextFormatter.normalizeSpeechQuery()</code> engine. Common spoken terms are converted to proper scientific formatting:
</p>
<div class="formula-box">
  "s n 1 reaction" &rarr; "S_N1 reaction"<br>
  "huckel 4 n plus 2 rule" &rarr; "Hückel (4n+2) π-electron rule"<br>
  "proton n m r splitting" &rarr; "¹H NMR splitting pattern"<br>
  "diels alder reaction" &rarr; "Diels-Alder [4+2] cycloaddition"
</div>

<h3>3.4 Multi-Key Gemini AI Orchestrator</h3>
<p>
  To guarantee 99.9% uptime and prevent Google Gemini rate limits (HTTP 429), ChemBuddy utilizes an intelligent key-pool orchestrator:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Round-Robin Key Rotation:</strong> Distributes requests across multiple API keys.</li>
  <li><strong>Automatic Failover:</strong> If a key reaches its quota, the app automatically fails over to the next key without alerting the user.</li>
  <li><strong>Model Fallback Hierarchy:</strong> Automatically tries <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code> &rarr; <code>gemini-2.0-flash</code> &rarr; <code>gemini-1.5-flash</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Offline Synthesizer:</strong> If completely offline, the local reaction engine and textbook databases take over seamlessly.</li>
</ul>

