<!-- CHAPTER 5 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>5. Smart Timetable & Attendance Intelligence Engine</h2>

<div class="two-column">
  <div class="column-text">
    <p>
      The attendance module uses predictive mathematical equations to keep students compliant with the university 75.0% threshold.
    </p>

    <h3>5.1 The 75% Cutoff Mathematics</h3>
    <p><strong>1. Classes Needed to Recover 75%:</strong></p>
    <div class="formula-box">
      $$	ext{Needed} = \max\left(0, \lceil 3 	imes 	ext{Absent} - 	ext{Present} ceilight)$$
    </div>
    <p>
      Indicates the exact consecutive classes required without a single absence to reach 75.0%.
    </p>

    <p><strong>2. Safe Bunks Available:</strong></p>
    <div class="formula-box">
      $$	ext{Can Skip} = \max\left(0, \lfloor (	ext{Present} - 3 	imes 	ext{Absent}) / 3 flooright)$$
    </div>
    <p>
      Shows how many classes can be safely skipped while remaining strictly above 75.0%.
    </p>

    <h3>5.2 Attendance States</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Present (&check;):</strong> Increments both Present and Total counts.</li>
      <li><strong>Absent (&cross;):</strong> Increments Total count only.</li>
      <li><strong>Postponed / Cancelled (&par;):</strong> <strong>Excluded from calculations.</strong> Does not penalize your percentage when a professor is absent or a holiday occurs.</li>
      <li><strong>On Duty (OD):</strong> Treated as Present for official university events.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="column-image">
    <div class="screenshot-container">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64," class="screenshot-img" alt="Timetable and Attendance Screen">
