<!-- CHAPTER 9 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>9. Spectroscopy & Chromatography Hub & Structure Solver</h2>

<div class="two-column">
  <div class="column-text">
    <p>
      The <strong>Spectroscopy Hub</strong> covers 8 major analytical techniques and features an intelligent Structure Solver capable of identifying unknown compounds from spectroscopic data.
    </p>

    <h3>9.1 8 Analytical Techniques</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>RP-HPLC & GC:</strong> Retention times, plate counts (N), resolution (Rs).</li>
      <li><strong>500 MHz <sup>1</sup>H NMR & <sup>13</sup>C DEPT:</strong> Chemical shifts, multiplicity, coupling constants (J), DEPT-45/90/135.</li>
      <li><strong>FT-IR:</strong> Characteristic functional group frequencies (carbonyls, O-H, N-H, triple bonds).</li>
      <li><strong>Mass Spectrometry:</strong> Molecular ion peak (M<sup>+</sup>), base peak, McLafferty rearrangement.</li>
      <li><strong>UV-Vis:</strong> Woodward-Fieser rules for conjugated dienes and enones.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>9.2 Structure Solver Intelligence (52+ Molecules)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Double Bond Equivalent (DBE):</strong> Automatically computes degrees of unsaturation from molecular formula.</li>
      <li><strong>Constitutional Isomer Ruling-Out:</strong> Explains systematically why alternative isomers are excluded based on coupling patterns and chemical shifts.</li>
      <li><strong>Interactive Zoom (1.0x - 5.0x):</strong> Smooth pan and zoom with haptic peak snapping.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="column-image">
    <div class="screenshot-container">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64," class="screenshot-img" alt="Spectroscopy & Structure Solver">
      <div class="screenshot-caption">Figure 9.1: Spectroscopy Solver analyzing Aspirin (C9H8O4, DBE=6.0) with zoomable 1H NMR spectrum and isomer exclusion rationale.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- CHAPTER 10 & 11 -->
<h2>10. MSc Chemistry Toolkit & 16 Postgrad Calculators</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy includes 16 specialized postgrad calculators organized into 6 practical laboratory domains:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Solutions & Concentrations:</strong> Molar Mass, Molarity (g/L & M), Dilution (<code>C1*V1 = C2*V2</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Acid-Base & Buffers:</strong> pH/pOH, Henderson-Hasselbalch, Buffer Formulation Assistant (Acetate, Phosphate).</li>
  <li><strong>Thermodynamics & Kinetics:</strong> Gibbs Free Energy (<code>ΔG = ΔH - TΔS</code>), Arrhenius Rate Law (Activation Energy <code>Ea</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Spectroscopy:</strong> Beer-Lambert Law (<code>A = ε*c*l</code>), Photon Energy (<code>E = h*c / λ</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Electrochemistry:</strong> Nernst Equation (<code>E = E° - (RT/nF)*ln(Q)</code>), Standard Cell Potential.</li>
  <li><strong>Chromatography:</strong> HPLC Calibration Curve (<code>y = mx + c</code>), Theoretical Plates (<code>N = 16*(tR/W)^2</code>), Resolution (<code>Rs</code>), Kovats Retention Index (<code>I</code>).</li>
</ul>

<h2>11. Pericyclic Hub & Woodward-Hoffmann FMO Engine</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Frontier Molecular Orbital (FMO) Theory:</strong> Visualizes HOMO and LUMO symmetry under thermal (Δ) and photochemical (hν) conditions.</li>
  <li><strong>Electrocyclic Reactions:</strong> 4n systems (Thermal: Conrotatory, Photo: Disrotatory) and 4n+2 systems (Thermal: Disrotatory, Photo: Conrotatory).</li>
  <li><strong>Cycloadditions:</strong> [4+2] Diels-Alder (Suprafacial-Suprafacial) and [2+2] Photocycloadditions.</li>
  <li><strong>Sigmatropic Rearrangements:</strong> [1,3], [1,5], and [3,3] Cope and Claisen rearrangements.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 12 & 13 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>12. Smart Flashcards & Spaced Repetition (Active Recall)</h2>

<div class="two-column">
  <div class="column-text">
    <p>
      The <strong>Smart Flashcards</strong> engine implements the scientifically proven <strong>SuperMemo-2 (SM-2)</strong> spaced repetition algorithm to guarantee long-term retention of reaction mechanisms, reagents, and spectroscopic values.
    </p>

    <h3>12.1 4-Point Confidence Ratings</h3>
    <p>After flipping a card to reveal the answer, rate your recall:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong style="color: #EF4444;">Again (1):</strong> Interval resets to &lt;1 day.</li>
      <li><strong style="color: #F59E0B;">Hard (2):</strong> Modest interval increase (~3 days).</li>
      <li><strong style="color: #3B82F6;">Good (3):</strong> Standard exponential increase (~6 days).</li>
      <li><strong style="color: #10B981;">Easy (4):</strong> Maximum interval increase (~12+ days).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>12.2 Auto-Deck Generation</h3>
    <p>
      Tap <strong>"Save as Flashcard"</strong> on any response inside Ask ChemBuddy AI or import a syllabus PDF to automatically generate a tailored flashcard deck with questions and model answers.
    </p>
  </div>

